// Run locally with `wrangler dev` (4.162.0, local R2 and Durable Object). Deployed with `wrangler deploy` from `main`, after `pnpm build:web` (first deploy 2026-11-16). The
// secrets (HMAC_SECRET, which every request needs; ADMIN_TOKEN, for `/admin`; TURNSTILE_SECRET) go in `.dev.vars` locally (copy `.dev.vars.example`) and in `wrangler secret put`
// when deployed; `TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` when Turnstile is on. PlaySession (another spec) is added with its spec;
// PartyRoom and PartyDirectory serve `/api/party` (party mode; `PARTY_ENABLED` off closes it).
// The web app: the Worker serves `../web/dist` (build it first: `pnpm build:web`, or `pnpm dev:app` to build and run). `run_worker_first` sends every request
// through the Worker, so every page carries the Content-Security-Policy (naming Turnstile only when it is configured; a static headers file could not) and
// `/api/*` and `/admin/*` are never answered with a page. The Worker passes every other GET and HEAD to the `ASSETS` binding (`api/src/http/assets.ts`),
// and `not_found_handling` makes the binding answer `index.html` for a page that is not a file, so a link such as `/shared/<id>` opens the app. Each file
// request is then a Worker request; that is the price of the policy on the page.
// The Workers AI binding (`AI`) is declared below (2026-11-16) so the ghost's voice can work. THE VOICE IS STILL OFF: it speaks only while the operator has opened a window
// (`POST /admin/voice`, minutes and a line cap, closing by itself; `docs/VOICE-WINDOW.md`). The Place Brief check (a photo must pass it before a world can be made from it) and
// the sketch (drawing a place) read the same binding, but they run only when world making is on (`WLT_API_KEY`, below) and the narrator only with `AI_GATEWAY_ID`: neither
// is set. In `wrangler dev` the binding always reaches the real service (a `wrangler login` and a small charge per call).
// The ghost's text, the free-text check (Llama Guard) and the portrait cut-out are built too (`WorkersAiClient`), with no route to use them yet. The first two use
// the same `AI` binding; the cut-out needs the Images binding, `"images": { "binding": "IMAGES" }` (an Images Paid subscription, and `wrangler dev --remote`:
// the default offline copy of the binding cannot remove a background). The Images binding is not declared until you decide to spend (`docs/spikes/1.2.md`).
// World making is off until `WLT_API_KEY` is set (a secret: `.dev.vars` locally, `wrangler secret put` if ever deployed; see `.dev.vars.example`).
{
  "name": "hauntology",
  "main": "src/worker.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-06-01",
  "assets": { "directory": "../web/dist", "binding": "ASSETS", "not_found_handling": "single-page-application", "run_worker_first": true },
  "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "BUCKET", "bucket_name": "hauntology-worlds" }],
  "ai": { "binding": "AI" },
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "WORLD_JOB", "class_name": "WorldJob" },
      { "name": "SPEND_GUARD", "class_name": "SpendGuard" },
      // Party mode: one Room per code (sockets hibernate), one directory for the caps.
      { "name": "PARTY_ROOM", "class_name": "PartyRoom" },
      { "name": "PARTY_DIRECTORY", "class_name": "PartyDirectory" },
      // The ghost's games: one PlaySession for each game (named by its unguessable id), one PlayIndex listing the games of each world so deleting a place deletes them.
      { "name": "PLAY_SESSION", "class_name": "PlaySession" },
      { "name": "PLAY_INDEX", "class_name": "PlayIndex" }
    ]
  },
  "migrations": [
    { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["WorldJob"] },
    { "tag": "v2", "new_sqlite_classes": ["SpendGuard"] },
    { "tag": "v3", "new_sqlite_classes": ["PartyRoom", "PartyDirectory"] },
    { "tag": "v4", "new_sqlite_classes": ["PlaySession", "PlayIndex"] }
  ],
  // Hourly: delete uploads past 24 hours and user worlds past 7 days.
  "triggers": { "crons": ["17 * * * *"] },
  // World making is live (WLT_API_KEY is set on the Worker) at the default model and the default day (10) and total (30) caps. Per visitor: 5 worlds for one Session (WORLD_SESSION_CAP,
  // default 2) and 5 a day for one hashed address (WORLD_IP_DAY_CAP, off unless set), so one person cannot use the day up, whatever cookies they clear. `POST /admin/kill {"on": true}` closes it at once.
  "vars": { "WORLD_GEN_ENABLED": "true", "UPLOAD_TTL_HOURS": "24", "WORLD_TTL_DAYS": "7", "WORLD_SESSION_CAP": "5", "WORLD_IP_DAY_CAP": "5" }
}
